// .mcp.json — Claude Code project-scoped MCP server config.
// Copy this file to `.mcp.json` and edit. `.mcp.json` is gitignored
// so the bearer token does not leak via git.
//
// ─── Required fields ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Claude Code requires both "type" and "url" on every server entry.
// "type" must be "http" (or "sse" / "ws" for those transports); without
// it Claude Code prints "Skipped — has a url but no type" and the server
// never connects. "transport" is set in addition for documentation but
// is inferred from "type" when omitted.
//
// ─── Token handling ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// By default the Authorization header references the
// WAN_IP_CHECK_MCP_TOKEN environment variable. Set it in your shell
// before launching Claude Code:
//
//     export WAN_IP_CHECK_MCP_TOKEN="<your token>"
//     claude
//
// This is the safest pattern — the token never lands in any file
// Claude Code reads.
//
// If you prefer a literal token in the file (e.g. for a shared CI
// runner where the env var can't be set per-invocation), replace the
// `${WAN_IP_CHECK_MCP_TOKEN}` placeholder below with the token
// directly.
//
// ─── Endpoint ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// Replace the URL below with your wan-ip-check host. Common options:
//
//     http://localhost:7374/mcp                # local dev (same machine)
//     http://your-hostname.local:7374/mcp      # LAN / mDNS
//     https://wanip.example.com/mcp            # behind a reverse proxy
//
// ─── What's exposed ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// See README.md § "MCP Server for AI Agents" for the full tool list.
// All 6 tools are read-only (no destructive writes). Secrets returned
// by list_actions are masked via the existing maskSecrets helper.
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "wan-ip-check": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "http://localhost:7374/mcp",
      "transport": "streamable-http",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Bearer ${WAN_IP_CHECK_MCP_TOKEN}"
      }
    }
  }
}